"59dd73f5-4253-480f-ac67-1a06fb7895e9","position":{"commit_sha":"8d08c7d8bde9a6dc86b8040f8820e16c829de6fc","position":"1786505028084879001-59dd73f5-4253-480f-ac67-1a06fb7895e9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## THIRD CONTRADICTED ENTRY — and this one is a SAME-DIGEST contradiction, which sharpens the argument\n\nRetracted on `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` in Gerrit **1394** (patchset 2).\n\n**The claim:** [req-0022] — \"two distinct issue-type ids (10003 and 10004) are both named `Task`,\nso name-based type resolution is ambiguous\".\n\n**The measurement:** harness run **30951453979** (`main` @ `d394a70529`), `GET\n/rest/api/2/issuetype` → HTTP 200, `[2e47-issue-type-evidence]`:\n\n    instance-wide entries matching ['Task','Sub-task','Epic']:\n      [('10002', 'Task'), ('10003', 'Sub-task'), ('10000', 'Epic')]\n\nExactly **one** id named `Task`, and **10003 is `Sub-task`, not `Task`**. The emitter\n(`tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py`) filters the full `/issuetype` response on those three\nnames with **no de-duplication**, so a second `Task` would have printed had one existed.\n\n## Why this is the strongest evidence yet for a deterministic re-measurement pass\n\nThe running tally of map entries contradicted by live measurement is now **three**:\n\n| entry | claim | measured | retracted in |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| req-0071/0072/0073 | DC rejects a 255-char label (ceiling 254) | 254 **and** 255 accepted, read back | 1389 |\n| req-0022 | ids 10003 + 10004 both named `Task` | one `Task` (10002); 10003 = `Sub-task` | 1394 ps2 |\n| — | description/comment ceiling | never observed at all; only read as *configured* | open (AC3 here) |\n\n**The load-bearing detail: the digest was IDENTICAL.** The `FROM` pin at `d394a70529` is\nbyte-identical to the one the map records, so run 30951453979 measured the same pinned base image\nthe answers describe. This is therefore **not** base-image drift — it is precisely the failure\nmode this ticket exists for: **a wrong answer at an unchanged digest**, which the new digest gate\nprovably cannot catch.\n\nThat is worth being exact about, because it upgrades the argument from \"the map could go stale\" to\n\"the map has been wrong twice on the image we actually run, and neither instance was detectable by\nany check we had\". The digest gate landed in 259b is still what makes this *diagnosable* — with the\npin asserted, \"different image\" is ruled out mechanically rather than argued — but ruling out one\nexplanation is not the same as detecting the defect.\n\n**What remains undetermined**, and deliberately not overstated in the doc: issue-type ids are\nassigned as instance state is built, and the mapping run created a project from **each** candidate\ntemplate while the harness provisions a **single** Scrum project. So the map's reading may reflect\ninstance state its own broader provisioning produced rather than a misreading of its evidence.\nEither way the *conclusion* does not hold for the environment the harness runs.\n\n**This tightens AC1 here:** a deterministic pass must re-assert claims **against the provisioning\nstate it declares**, not merely against the image digest. Two runs of the same image with\ndifferent provisioning are not comparable, and an id-valued claim is not portable between them —\nwhich is an argument for the contract pinning issue types by NAME-to-ID resolution performed at\nsetup, rather than recording raw ids as facts about \"the image\".","timestamp":1785884632495086001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Residual: a stale in-code assertion of the retracted req-0022 claim\n\nRecording so it is not lost. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:486-497` still carries a\ncomment asserting the duplicate-`Task` finding as FACT. With req-0022 retracted in Gerrit 1394 ps2,\nthat comment now contradicts the doc, and it sits ~10 lines above the evidence emitter (`:499-534`)\nthat produced the contradicting measurement — so the next reader gets the refuted claim and its\nrefutation from the same file.\n\n**Deliberately NOT fixed yet, and by whom:** that file is inside the blast radius of the in-flight\nDC parent-hierarchy stream ([rebar:9f26-66c2-14af-4223] / [rebar:4b9e-bcad-456a-4233]). Editing it\nnow risks a conflict for a comment-only change, and interrupting that stream to reconcile a comment\nis a bad trade. I own it and will land it once the hierarchy stream is in.\n\n**Verified independently** (not taken from a report): the recorded digest in the doc, the Dockerfile\npin in 1394 ps2, and the pin at `d394a70529` (the commit run 30951453979 ran) are all\n`sha256:04326628dc4ac36b2bfc1d0f2ebe5ba3807c1ec9cf9b18307d3c2ad7222537e9` — byte-identical. So this\nis a SAME-DIGEST contradiction and base-image drift is ruled out mechanically. My earlier framing of\nit as probable image drift was wrong.\n\nThat is the point this ticket exists for: two of the three contradicted claims were wrong about the\nimage we actually run, and neither was detectable by any check that existed. A digest gate answers\n'is this a different image', which is necessary and insufficient.","timestamp":1785884860917209001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR 2026-08-12: promoted to epic. Coordinator recommendation on urgency (operator asked): NOT urgent — the capability map gates no live decision today; parked as idea until a harness decision next depends on a mapped claim. Exception: the S4 docs-cleanup child (stale two-Task comment at tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:615) is unblocked and cheap — file it as an open child when convenient. Decomposition per triage: S1 machine-readable contract keyed to provisioning state; S2 deterministic no-LLM re-assertion script; S3 amd64 live 32767-ceiling measurement; S4 docs cleanup.","timestamp":1786505004462840001}],"created_at":1785884055478458001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4530bd41-d5eb-47b8-81c7-5a7e3c6bb0a3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"259b-b7da-a346-4785"},{"link_uuid":"f37ced4f-c17e-4b4d-8611-9e00872686b9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb"}],"description":"# Discovered while closing the map-staleness gap on [rebar:259b-b7da-a346-4785] (Gerrit 1394)\n\n259b now makes the capability map's **provenance** checkable: `run_metadata.json` derives the\nharness digest from the Dockerfile's `FROM` line instead of a hand-copied constant, and\n`docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` records the digest it was measured against, asserted against\nthat pin by `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py`. A re-pin now lands red until\nthe map is regenerated.\n\n## What that does NOT cover\n\nThe staleness gate keys on the **digest**. It detects \"these answers describe a different\nimage\". It cannot detect **\"these answers are wrong about THIS image\"** — and that is the\nfailure mode this epic has actually hit:\n\n* `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` recorded that DC rejected a 255-char label. A dedicated live\n  cell later posted 254- and 255-char labels to the SAME pinned image and both were accepted.\n  The entry was retracted. The digest never changed, so no digest-based check could have caught\n  it.\n\nThe mechanism is that the map's answers are produced by an **agentic LLM run** summarising raw\nREST evidence. The evidence in `evidence.json` was correct; the *reading* of it was wrong. So\nthe map has a trust boundary at exactly the point the ticket wanted removed — 259b's own words:\n\"otherwise we have swapped 'discovering from the instance' for 'trusting a model', which is\nworse.\"\n\n## The shape of a fix (not prescribing it)\n\nA **deterministic, non-LLM re-measurement** pass: a script that reads the committed contract and\nre-asserts each claim with a fixed REST call and an exact comparison, exiting non-zero on\ndivergence — no model in the measurement path. `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py`\n(bug 1019) is the existing precedent for a deterministic probe alongside the agentic map, and\n`_assert_project_capabilities` in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is the precedent for\n\"declared contract, fail loudly on divergence\". The agentic run stays useful for DISCOVERY (open\nquestions, new checklist items); it just should not be the last word on a value the harness then\ndepends on.\n\n## Also recorded: one measurement gap left open by 259b\n\n`docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` notes the description/comment 32767 boundary is a **coverage\ngap** — `jira.text.field.character.limit=32767` was read from the instance, but a literal 32K+\npayload was never written, so the limit is confirmed as *configured*, not as *observed*. That\nneeds an amd64 live run; it cannot be settled from a dev worktree.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] every claim the harness DEPENDS on is re-assertable by a deterministic (no-LLM) pass whose\n      comparison is exact, and which exits non-zero on divergence\n- [ ] the pass is runnable against the pinned image on demand, and its failure message names the\n      committed claim that diverged\n- [ ] the description/comment ceiling is measured with a real over-limit payload and read-back,\n      closing the recorded coverage gap\n- [ ] the agentic map's role is documented as DISCOVERY, with the deterministic pass as the\n      authority for anything the harness relies on","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","e369-a449-4773-48fb"],["relates_to","e369-a449-4773-48fb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"59dd73f5-4253-480f-ac67-1a06fb7895e9","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"idea","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a9bd-6641-e603-42bc","ticket_type":"epic","title":"The capability map's answers are LLM-summarised, so a wrong answer at an unchanged digest is still undetectable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["44837f9b-e231-45e5-b39f-becb8e4fea12","4530bd41-d5eb-47b8-81c7-5a7e3c6bb0a3","f47726fa-1583-40d6-8bd3-a58e12f9f33c","274ca539-27df-4516-9afd-e5083ae2002b","568203a5-1a12-4eee-b0b1-314a2a896dde","b74ebb45-d17e-419f-be88-8deb07acc4a6","f37ced4f-c17e-4b4d-8611-9e00872686b9","10ccd64a-6ca7-4311-9f94-2b4371e1619f","4d70bd0e-8e17-4b85-a517-142c389febf0","7871341f-f717-4e9b-854f-be44a6e30f11","5ad15880-386e-45da-a8d0-60695f092b81","abce8ab4-590e-4b78-b237-0e83a0ac3eda","0097181a-0964-455d-bac1-4416706184e4","59dd73f5-4253-480f-ac67-1a06fb7895e9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659648688437001,"uuid":"c6b8a25f-7fab-4c4e-bf5d-fc7ad4d1bc0c"}